lines=['# Kalshi full-market evaluation — September 26, 2026','','This replaces the earlier unsupported gold 15-minute allocation recommendation. No money was transferred and no orders or production changes were made.','','## What was actually evaluated','',f"Fresh catalog: 14,392 series across 20 categories; 14,464 standard open events fetched to cursor exhaustion, containing {struct['markets']:,} active markets after filtering. A separate 1,000-record recent combo sample and all 25 perpetual contracts were inspected. The combo universe was not exhaustively enumerated.",'',f"Fresh prediction diagnostics cover {validation['series']} series, {validation['market_rows']:,} downloaded settled market rows and {validation['candle_records']:,} candle records. There are {len(a)} declared prediction rule/series combinations, each with an optimistic opening-quote proxy and an adverse-latency closing-quote replay, plus {len(perps)} perpetual combinations. There are {audit['hypotheses']} primary hypotheses in the selection audit. These are **candidate screens and explicitly defined strategy tests**, not proof that every possible strategy on every market was tested.",'','Every catalog series has an assessment in `results/series_assessments.jsonl`. The category and model-level dispositions are in `family_review.md`. An inactive or data-insufficient market is labeled that way, not falsely assigned a simulated profit.','','## Decision','','No new strategy is approved for live allocation from this review. Several have positive simulated returns, but none combines sufficiently independent validation, demonstrated executable depth and reliable tail-risk evidence. The strongest new lead is **gold perpetual six-hour mean reversion**, a different product and rule from the rejected gold 15-minute allocation. Its positive 15-day sample survives a minute-quote delay challenge, but it is a post-selection lead rather than a proven edge. Positive weather and commodity results should be read with their date coverage, chronological halves and cost sensitivity below; rankings based only on gross profit are rejected.','','## Prediction-market results','','All dollars below use two contracts per candidate trade. These are isolated strategy tests, not additive profits across bots. The opening proxy buys at the worse of signal ask and next-bar opening ask, within the one-cent limit; its exact live availability is unproved. The delayed variant uses the following bar close (one minute for short-duration/weather; one hour for daily diagnostics), which can be harsher than normal latency. Both include current per-series modeled taker fees. +1c/+2c means additional cost **per contract**. No historical depth or queue priority is inferred.','','| Series / rule | Trades | Days | Net after fees | +1c cost | +2c cost | +1c first / second half | +1c max DD | Delayed +1c | $100 portfolio end* | Delayed portfolio end* |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
for r in a:
 u=r['unconstrained'];v=b[(r['series'],r['rule'])]['unconstrained'];n=u.get('trades',0)
 halves=f"{dollars(u.get('first_half_stress1'))} / {dollars(u.get('second_half_stress1'))}"
 lines.append(f"| {r['series']} / {r['rule']} | {n} | {u.get('days',0)} | {dollars(u.get('net'))} | {dollars(u.get('stress1'))} | {dollars(u.get('stress2'))} | {halves} | {dollars(u.get('max_drawdown_stress1'))} | {dollars(v.get('stress1'))} | ${r['portfolio']['ending_cash']:.2f} | ${b[(r['series'],r['rule'])]['portfolio']['ending_cash']:.2f} |")
lines+=['','*Each portfolio uses its indicated execution mode and +1c stress, $30 reserve, one unsettled two-contract position, $2.02 exposure ceiling, $4 daily worst-case-loss budget and $10 high-water drawdown budget. Settlement proceeds are reusable only at recorded settlement time. A profitable capped path does not rescue a negative general strategy: stopping/skipping changes the sample. We do not select a bot because a particular stop happened to avoid later losses.','','Rules: `quote85` = 85–93c favorite ask, spread <=2c, 3–10 minutes left, no underlying filter. `stable93` = 93–99c favorite midpoint, <=1c spread, unbroken complete observed favorite path, 4–8 minutes left and at least five observations. `xrp80` and `zec95` are the previously reported XRP/ZEC path candidates under the current conservative implementation. `daily93` = 93–99c ask, <=2c spread, three same-favorite hourly observations, target eight hours before close. `weather85` = 85–93c ask, <=2c spread, five same-favorite minute observations, 15–45 minutes left. These market-price hypotheses do not constitute a weather/AAA/Pyth source forecasting model. Full specifications are frozen in PLAN.md and replay.py.','','## Perpetual results','','Fresh authenticated read-only fee checks found crypto maker/taker rates of 2/12bp per side and metals maker/taker rates of 0.12/0.72bp per side for this account. The old archived 80bp taker assumption is obsolete. These tests use taker fees, not optimistic maker fills. They include actual public funding records, bid/ask crossing and extra one tick or one basis point per side (whichever is larger). Fees are current-rate scenarios, not historical fee reconstruction.','','Maximum $50 entry notional in whole contracts; no leverage multiplier. Signals compare completed mid quotes over six or 24 hours and execute at the next hourly opening quote proxy, with a fixed six-/24-hour exit. No historical depth or intrabar liquidation simulation is asserted. Below are **all 75 combinations**, including unavailable-data rows.','','| Contract / rule | Trades | Days | Net incl. fees/funding | Extra execution stress | Stress first / second half | Closed-trade max DD | Raw day-bootstrap 5% mean/trade |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|---:|---:|']
for r in perps:
 lines.append(f"| {r['ticker']} / {r['rule']} | {r['trades']} | {r['days']} | {dollars(r['net'])} | {dollars(r['stress'])} | {dollars(r['first_half_stress'])} / {dollars(r['second_half_stress'])} | {dollars(r['max_drawdown_stress'])} | {dollars(r['bootstrap_p05_per_trade'])} |")
lines+=['','Gold perpetual challenge: same selected six-hour reversal signals, use actual minute bid/ask closes 60 seconds after both scheduled entry and exit. '+f"{challenge['trades']} trades, {challenge['missing']} missing, net {dollars(challenge['net'])}, stressed {dollars(challenge['stress'])}, closed-trade stressed drawdown {dollars(challenge['max_drawdown'])}. This is a **post-selection execution challenge on the same dates**, not an independent holdout.",'','## Why positive rows are not automatic approvals','','The selection audit applies a 10,000-draw day-block sign-randomization diagnostic and reports BH and Bonferroni adjustments across every declared primary hypothesis. Sign symmetry and day independence are assumptions; these p-values are exploratory diagnostics, not financial guarantees. Basic bootstrap bounds also omit unseen tail events and cross-day dependence. No unadjusted 5% bound is treated as a discovery after testing many ideas.','','All-win samples get a separate lower win-probability calculation. For example, a few dozen wins bought near 97–99c cannot establish the needed >97–99% true success rate. Correlated trades make the effective sample smaller still. Rule/data changes, short listing history, historical fee assumptions, missing depth, future source revisions and post-selection reuse are disclosed. The new weather extension reused rules after examining its initial week; its result is not described as untouched out-of-sample evidence.','','## Structural price check','',f"Examined {struct['coverage'].get('exclusive_no_examined',0):,} mutually-exclusive NO basket groups; {struct['coverage'].get('exclusive_no_priced',0):,} had displayed two-contract prices on every leg. Examined {struct['coverage'].get('threshold_examined',0):,} cheapest eligible lower-threshold versus upper-NO comparisons; {struct['coverage'].get('threshold_priced',0):,} were priceable. Found {len(struct['opportunities'])} positive fee-inclusive opportunities under these machine-verifiable scopes and the $70 spend limit. The paginated snapshot is not atomic. Generic cross-event correlations, unverified scopes and exhaustive combinations are not claimed as tested arbitrage.",'','## All-category coverage','','| Category | Catalog series | Active series | Active markets | Tight two-sided 2-contract markets |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
for cat,c in sorted(cats.items()):lines.append(f"| {cat} | {c['catalog_series']:,} | {c['open_series']:,} | {c['markets']:,} | {c['tight_two_contract_markets']:,} |")
lines+=['','## Data and audit boundaries','',f"Validation: {len(validation['errors'])} errors; {validation['missing_records']} missing requested candle records; {validation['empty_candle_histories']} empty candle histories excluded from signal generation. Nine replay unit tests cover chronology, fee arithmetic, future-label invariance, pending exposure, loss budgets and timestamps. Empty histories do not imply lack of trading. Available perps history varies from zero to about 49 days; gold/silver about 15 days and platinum/palladium about two days.",'','Most 15-minute and hourly-weather tests cover markets closing September 8–25; daily/weekly diagnostics use August 8–September 25 where available. Entry timestamps can fall on the preceding UTC date. Some September commodity dates were examined in prior work: they are reused evidence, not a clean discovery holdout. Current settled metadata was used; an as-of metadata archive was not reconstructed. Next-bar quoted prices do not establish executable depth. All raw inputs, rejected variants, trades, fees, skipped portfolio events and availability counts are retained.','','## Primary sources','','- [Kalshi market API](https://docs.kalshi.com/api-reference/market/get-markets)','- [Kalshi fee schedule](https://kalshi.com/docs/kalshi-fee-schedule.pdf)','- [Perps fees and funding explanation](https://help.kalshi.com/en/articles/16071417-perps-fees-explained)','- [Perpetual market API](https://docs.kalshi.com/margin-rest/market/get-markets)','- [Perpetual candles](https://docs.kalshi.com/margin-rest/market/get-market-candlesticks)','- [Pyth live-feed documentation](https://docs.kalshi.com/websockets/pyth-value)','- [Pyth history access](https://docs.pyth.network/price-feeds/pro/api/history)','','The public API payloads and authenticated fee-rate receipt in this package support the fresh numbers. Prior reports are background only and are not presented as newly verified profits.']
